{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"fiedlerVector","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalized","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = false, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1e-8, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FiedlerVector","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/FiedlerVector","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory13FiedlerVectorV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization, the null space projected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, from a fixed start vector: on σI − L (σ twice the largest weighted degree; 2I − N with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalized"},{"type":"text","text":") while σ\/λ₂ is moderate, else on L⁺ by shift-invert, each product a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conjugate-gradient solve with L grounded at the vertex of largest degree. A Ritz pair is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accepted when its residual is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · λ₂, so λ₂ is relative to itself however"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the weights spread; the value is then the vector’s Rayleigh quotient, a sum over edges. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver below 64 vertices. O((n + m) · products) time; 31 n "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s (34 n from 5,000"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, for the polynomial filter), and on the shift-invert path O(n + m) more for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solver."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"At least two vertices, ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance > 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", when given, is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at least 1.","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Throws","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when the Lanczos run on L⁺ spends "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" matrix–vector"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"products (1,000 when nil) without converging, with the products spent and the Ritz"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"residual relative to 1\/λ₂. The run on σI − L that may come first hands over to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shift-invert rather than throwing, after 4,000 + 20√n products or "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whichever is smaller. Each shift-invert product is a conjugate-gradient solve that throws,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with its own iterations and relative residual, after 20,000 + 2n. Below 64 vertices the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dense solver answers and "},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is unused. Only a tolerance below rounding has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reached the default limits in the measurements."}]}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P08SpectralA6TheoryE13fiedlerVector10normalized9tolerance13maxIterationsAD07FiedlerF0VyxGSgSb_SdSiSgtAA13NoConvergenceVYKF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"fiedlerVector(normalized:tolerance:maxIterations:)","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"fiedlerVector"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"normalized","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FiedlerVector","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:19SpectralGraphTheory13FiedlerVectorV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"FiedlerVector.swift","url":"https:\/\/gi